        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "931e5fdd-c856-54d3-adba-67e954ede061",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John McPhun, Jairos Jiri\n- Places: Rhodesia, Salisbury, Harare, Southern Rhodesia\n- Roles: first-class cricketer\n- Events: responsible government in 1923\n- Topics: disability support, Christian charity\n\nFacts:\n- Southern Rhodesia achieved responsible government in 1923.\n- Rhodesia, with its capital in Salisbury, was considered a de facto successor state to the former British colony of Southern Rhodesia.\n- Salisbury is now called Harare.\n- Jairos Jiri started creating facilities in the 1940s for disadvantaged and disabled people in Rhodesia/Zimbabwe.\n- Jairos Jiri used Christian principles of charity, patience, and non-judgmental tolerance in his work.\n- John David McPhun was born on September 8, 1940, in Salisbury, Rhodesia.\n- John David McPhun was a first-class cricketer who played for Rhodesia in the Currie Cup.",
